# CODEOWNERS — Schema & Security Governance
# ===========================================
# Files listed here require an approved review from @DonSquires before any
# Pull Request can be merged. This protects the live database schema, TypeScript
# type definitions, CI/CD workflows, and their governing documentation from
# accidental or unauthorised changes.
#
# HOW IT WORKS
# Any PR that touches a path matching a rule below will automatically request
# a review from the owner(s) listed. The PR cannot be merged until that review
# is approved (provided branch protection requires CODEOWNERS approval — see
# Settings → Branches → Require review from Code Owners).
#
# WHAT IS PROTECTED
# • Supabase migrations — direct schema changes to the live database
# • Supabase edge functions — server-side code that reads/writes the database
# • TypeScript type files — must stay in sync with the live schema
# • Schema documentation — authoritative reference for all developers and agents
# • GitHub Actions workflows — CI/CD pipelines that push to production
# • This file itself — prevents tampering with the governance rules

# ── Supabase migrations (any new or modified .sql file) ──────────────────────
/supabase/migrations/                  @DonSquires

# ── Supabase edge functions ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
/supabase/functions/                   @DonSquires

# ── TypeScript type definitions (must match live schema) ─────────────────────
/src/types/                            @DonSquires

# ── Authoritative live schema document ───────────────────────────────────────
/docs/LIVE_SCHEMA.md                   @DonSquires

# ── Schema validation checklist and codebase audit ───────────────────────────
/SCHEMA_VALIDATION_CHECKLIST.md        @DonSquires
/CODEBASE_AUDIT.txt                    @DonSquires
/AUDIT_INDEX.md                        @DonSquires
/AUDIT_EXECUTIVE_SUMMARY.md            @DonSquires

# ── GitHub Actions workflows (includes supabase-db-push.yml) ─────────────────
/.github/workflows/                    @DonSquires

# ── This file itself ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
/.github/CODEOWNERS                    @DonSquires
